      <h4>RFD 0042: Bounded retries for webhook deliveries</h4>
      <h5>Summary</h5>
      <p class="pv-chg mod">Today the dispatcher <span class="pv-hl">retries failed deliveries indefinitely</span><span class="pv-anchor a1"><span class="w-dot on"></span><span class="w-h on"></span><span class="pv-thread active pv-float">
        <span class="pv-c">
          <span class="pv-who"><span class="pv-av">PK</span><b>priya-k</b><span>2h</span></span>
          <span class="pv-q">retries failed deliveries indefinitely</span>
          Indefinitely? The proposal caps it at 8 tries. Should the summary say "until the cap"?
        </span>
        <span class="pv-foot"><span class="pv-gh">Review thread · L12</span><b>Reply · Resolve</b></span>
      </span></span>, which lets one broken endpoint hold a worker slot for days. This RFD proposes a bounded schedule with jitter and a <span class="pv-hl idle">dead-letter queue</span><span class="pv-anchor a2"><span class="w-dot"></span><span class="w-elbow"></span><span class="w-in"></span><span class="pv-thread pv-float">
        <span class="pv-c">
          <span class="pv-who"><span class="pv-av">JL</span><b>jlo</b><span>1d</span></span>
          <span class="pv-q">dead-letter queue</span>
          Who gets paged when this fills up?
        </span>
      </span></span>.</p>
      <h5>Proposal</h5>
      <p class="pv-chg add">After the final attempt, the event moves to the dead-letter queue.</p>
